---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/ifric/ifric16.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType="IFRS"
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s3", label: "What Risk Can Actually Be Hedged" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Presentation Currency Is Not an Exposure" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Where the Hedging Instrument Can Be Held" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Effectiveness Testing" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Amounts Reclassified on Disposal" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Intragroup Hedging Instrument" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "IFRIC 16 vs US GAAP" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Why net investment hedging needed specific guidance</div>
        <div class="principle">IAS 21 required net investment hedges to be treated differently from ordinary foreign currency hedges — the exchange differences on the hedged item go to other comprehensive income, and the exchange differences on the hedging instrument are ALSO reclassified to OCI. IFRIC 16 resolved remaining questions about WHICH instruments qualify, WHERE they can be held, and HOW amounts move on disposal — questions that IAS 21's general hedge accounting guidance did not fully answer.</div>
        <div class="note">Without IFRIC 16, entities could legitimately apply different net investment hedge treatments depending on the legal form of the hedging instrument — an inconsistency that undermined the comparability of financial statements across jurisdictions.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The unique economics of a net investment hedge</div>
        <div class="principle">A net investment hedge is not hedging a transaction or a recognised asset/liability directly — it is hedging the FOREIGN CURRENCY RISK on the CONSOLIDATED CARRYING AMOUNT of a foreign operation. The hedged item is effectively the net assets of the foreign subsidiary, measured in the parent's presentation currency. The economic exposure exists regardless of the legal structure of the group.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope & Definitions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What IFRIC 16 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 16 applies to HEDGE ACCOUNTING for a hedge of the foreign currency risk arising from a net investment in a FOREIGN OPERATION. The hedge may be designated against the foreign operation as a whole, or against the net investment in the foreign operation. The hedged item is always the net investment in the foreign operation, not the individual assets and liabilities within it.</div>
        <div class="elabel">TYPICAL FACT PATTERNS</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>A parent hedging the EUR net assets of a German subsidiary using EUR/USD forward contracts</span>
          <span>A group with multiple foreign operations hedging aggregate net investment risk using a basket of currencies</span>
          <span>An intragroup borrowing arrangement used as the hedging instrument</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Net investment in a foreign operation</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The carrying amount of the reporting entity's net assets (assets minus liabilities) in a foreign operation, as measured in the foreign operation's functional currency, translated into the reporting entity's presentation currency.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Hedging instrument</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A financial instrument (or group of instruments) designated as a hedge of the foreign currency risk on a net investment, which must be effective in offsetting the hedged risk.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>What Risk Can Actually Be Hedged</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">The specific risk that qualifies</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 16 clarifies that the ONLY risk that can be hedged under a net investment hedge is the FOREIGN CURRENCY RISK arising from the difference between the foreign operation's FUNCTIONAL CURRENCY and the PARENT'S PRESENTATION CURRENCY. Interest rate risk, credit risk, or other risks in the foreign operation CANNOT be hedged under this designation — they would need separate hedge accounting treatment.</div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--flush">⚠️ A common error is to try to hedge the "return on investment" risk or the "operational performance" risk of a foreign subsidiary. IFRIC 16 makes clear that ONLY the currency translation component of that risk qualifies for net investment hedge treatment.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Presentation Currency Is Not an Exposure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A common misconception dispelled</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 16 explicitly states that a difference in CURRENCIES that exists ONLY because the parent and the subsidiary have DIFFERENT PRESENTATION CURRENCIES (rather than different functional currencies) does NOT constitute a foreign currency risk that can be hedged. The exposure must arise from the TRANSLATION difference between the foreign operation's functional currency and the group's presentation currency.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Why this distinction matters</div>
        <div class="principle">If the parent's functional currency = the foreign subsidiary's functional currency, but the parent's PRESENTATION currency is different, the translation difference arises from the PRESENTATION CURRENCY choice — not from the economic risk of operating in a different currency. IFRIC 16 does NOT permit hedging of presentation currency differences.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Where the Hedging Instrument Can Be Held</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The intragroup borrowing solution</div>
        <div class="principle">One of IFRIC 16's most practically important conclusions is that the HEDGING INSTRUMENT CAN BE HELD BY ANY ENTITY WITHIN THE GROUP — not necessarily the parent. This means an intragroup borrowing arrangement between a SUBSIDIARY and the PARENT can qualify as the hedging instrument for the parent's net investment hedge of the SAME foreign operation. The instrument does NOT need to be a standalone derivative — a qualifying intragroup loan works.</div>
        <div class="elabel">KEY REQUIREMENTS</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>The intragroup borrowing must be denominated in the CURRENCY OF THE FOREIGN OPERATION being hedged</span>
          <span>The borrowing must be DESIGNATED as the hedging instrument — designation is not automatic</span>
          <span>Hedge accounting must be applied consistently — the intragroup borrowing cannot be treated as a hedge for consolidation purposes only</span>
        </div>
        <div class="callout info">This intragroup borrowing flexibility was specifically designed to allow groups to manage net investment hedge accounting efficiently without having to enter into external derivative contracts for every foreign operation.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Effectiveness Testing</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">The 80%-125% range</div>
        <div class="principle">Net investment hedges must pass the SAME EFFECTIVENESS TEST as other cash flow and fair value hedges: the hedge must be HIGHLY EFFECTIVE throughout the hedging relationship. IFRIC 16 notes that a net investment hedge is typically highly effective because the hedging instrument (e.g. a forward contract) and the hedged item (net investment) are both exposed to the same exchange rate.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Ongoing effectiveness assessment</div>
        <div class="principle">Effectiveness is assessed at each reporting date, prospectively and retrospectively. For net investment hedges, the practical challenge is that the hedged item is a BALANCE SHEET AMOUNT (the cumulative translation difference) while the hedging instrument may be measured at fair value through profit or loss — making the effectiveness comparison more complex than for a cash flow hedge.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Amounts Reclassified on Disposal</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">The reclassification mechanics on disposal of the foreign operation</div>
        <div class="principle">When a foreign operation is DISPOSED OF (or partially disposed), the cumulative amount of exchange differences recognised in other comprehensive income relating to that foreign operation MUST BE RECLASSIFIED from equity to profit or loss. IFRIC 16 clarifies that this reclassification occurs AT THE SAME TIME as the gain or loss on disposal is recognised — the cumulative OCI amount is released to profit or loss as a reclassification adjustment, not as a new gain or loss.</div>
        <div class="elabel">THE RECLASSIFICATION TIMING</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>Partial disposal: reclassify only the proportion of cumulative OCI relating to the disposed interest</span>
          <span>Full disposal: reclassify the ENTIRE cumulative OCI balance to profit or loss</span>
          <span>The reclassification adjustment is recognised IN THE SAME PERIOD as the disposal gain/loss</span>
        </div>
        <div class="formula-box">
          <div class="f-label">RECLASSIFICATION ON FULL DISPOSAL</div>
          <div class="f-eq">Gain/loss on disposal = Proceeds - carrying amount of net investment + cumulative OCI reclassified from equity (reclassification adjustment)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Intragroup Hedging Instrument</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="worked">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Intragroup EUR borrowing as a net investment hedge</div>
          <div class="wk-body">Parent Company (presentation currency: GBP) owns 100% of German Subsidiary (functional currency: EUR). At the start of the year, the parent borrows EUR 10m from the subsidiary as an intragroup loan, designated as the hedging instrument for the net investment in the German subsidiary. Exchange rate at inception: EUR/GBP 0.85. Exchange rate at year-end: EUR/GBP 0.82.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer"><strong>Step 1 — Hedged item:</strong> Net investment in German subsidiary = EUR 10m (carrying amount).<br><strong>Step 2 — Hedging instrument:</strong> Intragroup borrowing of EUR 10m, designated as hedge.<br><strong>Step 3 — Exchange rate movement:</strong> EUR 10m × (0.85 - 0.82) = EUR 300,000 GBP gain on translation.<br><strong>Step 4 — Hedge accounting:</strong> The GBP 300,000 gain on the hedged item (net investment) goes to OCI. The exchange difference on the intragroup borrowing ALSO goes to OCI (matching the hedged item).<br><strong>Step 5 — Effectiveness:</strong> The intragroup borrowing is 100% effective because it is denominated in the exact same currency (EUR) as the net investment being hedged.<br><strong>Step 6 — Consolidation:</strong> On consolidation, the intragroup borrowing and the net investment are eliminated, but the OCI amounts are NOT eliminated — they remain in equity until reclassified on disposal.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What IFRIC 16 requires (in addition to IFRS 7)</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Description of the hedging instrument, including its nominal amount and maturity</span>
          <span>Description of the hedged foreign operation</span>
          <span>The exchange risk being hedged and how the hedge is expected to affect it</span>
          <span>The extent to which hedge accounting was effective, with the range of hedge ratios used</span>
          <span>The amount reclassified from equity to profit or loss on disposal of the foreign operation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Whether the risk being hedged is specifically the foreign currency translation risk on the net investment (not other risks)</span>
              <span>Whether the hedging instrument is denominated in the correct currency and appropriately designated</span>
              <span>Whether an intragroup borrowing arrangement qualifies as a hedging instrument</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>The timing of a potential disposal of the foreign operation, affecting when cumulative OCI is reclassified</span>
              <span>The proportion of cumulative OCI to reclassify on partial disposal</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>IFRIC 16 vs US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — IFRIC 16 vs ASC 815 (Derivatives and Hedging)</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IFRIC 16 (IFRS)</span><span>US GAAP (ASC 815)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Qualifying risk</span><span>Foreign currency risk on net investment in foreign operation</span><span>Foreign currency risk on net investment in foreign operation</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Hedging instrument location</span><span>Can be held by any group entity (intragroup borrowing permitted)</span><span>Similar flexibility — intragroup transactions can qualify</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Hedged item</span><span>Net investment in foreign operation (consolidated net assets)</span><span>Net investment in foreign operation</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>OCI reclassification on disposal</span><span>Cumulative OCI reclassified to profit or loss on disposal</span><span>Same treatment — cumulative translation adjustment reclassified on disposal</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Presentation currency exclusion</span><span>Presentation currency differences do NOT qualify</span><span>Similar exclusion applies</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every IFRIC 16 event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Net investment translation difference (effective portion)</span><span><span class="badge bo">OCI</span></span><span>Recognised in other comprehensive income under IAS 21</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Hedging instrument gain/loss (effective portion)</span><span><span class="badge bo">OCI</span></span><span>Reclassified to OCI, matching the hedged item</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Cumulative OCI reclassified on disposal</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&L</span></span><span>Reclassification adjustment recognised in the same period as the disposal gain/loss</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Ineffective portion of hedge</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&L</span></span><span>Recognised immediately in profit or loss</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IAS 21</span><span>Governs functional currency determination and translation of foreign operations</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 9</span><span>Supplies the general hedge accounting model IFRIC 16 applies to net investment hedges</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 7</span><span>Governs disclosure of hedge accounting information</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 10</span><span>Supplies the group structure and consolidation basis</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Net investment hedge</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Hedge accounting treatment for the foreign currency risk on the net assets of a foreign operation, where both the hedged item and hedging instrument gains/losses are recognised in OCI.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Reclassification adjustment</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The amount transferred from equity (OCI) to profit or loss on disposal of a foreign operation, representing the cumulative exchange differences previously recognised in OCI.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Net investment in a foreign operation", definition: "The carrying amount of the reporting entity's net assets (assets minus liabilities) in a foreign operation, as measured in the foreign operation's functional currency and translated into the reporting entity's presentation currency." },
      { term: "Net investment hedge", definition: "Hedge accounting for the foreign currency risk on a net investment in a foreign operation, where the hedging instrument and hedged item gains/losses are recognised in other comprehensive income." },
      { term: "Reclassification adjustment", definition: "The transfer of cumulative exchange differences from equity (OCI) to profit or loss on disposal of a foreign operation." },
      { term: "Intragroup borrowing", definition: "A borrowing between group entities that can qualify as a hedging instrument for a net investment hedge under IFRIC 16." }
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.IFRIC16} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>




